{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SbibZnCZyv58wqHqN5yTk5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"a624af22d5816773b91f0c7768daa69617c73c24\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T16:12:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Support authentication failures from the backend (#1918)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b9884006387560e52219b747d953cac9fca2d05f\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:38:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Suppress Basic auth prompts for paginated REST requests (#1906)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-29T22:05:13+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5767: Redirect to Location header URL on session endpoint calls (#1797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"121793396a7ea5b449963e330f9eaaa6f510f375\",\"date\":\"2026-02-04T10:00:06-05:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Add doc strings to most of the undocumented functions in the API (#1575)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e31fe71dc33a99205effaec8ebb7450c5c9320a8\",\"date\":\"2025-07-24T14:47:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-4897 Redirect 401 request to URL location specified by resp… (#1430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-4897 Redirect 401 request to URL location specified by response header if frontend config URL is blank\\n\\n* *.md files\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3a27e7c23c9e77c4ee85a5b96f5260160e6e9cb8\",\"date\":\"2025-05-23T13:19:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Re-work Framework packages for lighter-weight builds (#1346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d6283b0981a23019a734f21a98485a4a0348cd27\",\"date\":\"2024-12-11T22:21:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Add FetchError interface for more granular error annotation (#1230)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR adds a `FetchError` interface to the framework that can be used to annotate errors that occur during fetch requests. It also amends the `OpenmrsFetchError` class to implement the `FetchError` interface.\\r\\n\\r\\nPresently, the openmrsFetch hook throws a custom `OpenmrsFetchError` class that includes the response status code and status text if a request fails. This is not always the most helpful message, and it's not always clear what the underlying error was.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe REST API returns a more useful message in the responseBody, and it would be preferable to show this message instead of the status code and status text